Relevant columns and why they matter  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."FromUserId": id of the voter – lets us know who is giving the up‑vote.  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."ToUserId": id of the receiver – lets us know who is getting the up‑vote.  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."ForumMessageId": unique post that received the vote – can be used with DISTINCT if we suspect duplicate rows.  
• USERS."Id": primary key that links users to their names.  
• USERS."UserName": concise user handle to show in the output.  
Conditions we will probably need  
• "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL AND "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL – ignore rows with missing values.  
• GROUP BY ("FromUserId", "ToUserId") – to count votes from one person to another.  
• JOIN the two opposite directions of the same pair to get the “up‑votes returned”.  
• ORDER BY received DESC, returned DESC, LIMIT 1 – to keep only the pair with the most one‑way votes.

Below are ten incremental Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that explore the data step‑by‑step and end with the final answer query.  
Every identifier is fully‑qualified and double‑quoted.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at the raw vote records.
SELECT *
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: How many votes has each user GIVEN?
SELECT "FromUserId",
       COUNT(*) AS "votes_given"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
WHERE "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "FromUserId"
ORDER BY "votes_given" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: How many votes has each user RECEIVED?
SELECT "ToUserId",
       COUNT(*) AS "votes_received"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
WHERE "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "ToUserId"
ORDER BY "votes_received" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Count votes for every FROM → TO pair.
SELECT "FromUserId",
       "ToUserId",
       COUNT(*) AS "pair_votes"
FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
WHERE "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
  AND "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "FromUserId", "ToUserId"
ORDER BY "pair_votes" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Save the pair counts to a CTE and look at the top 20.
WITH pair_cte AS (
    SELECT "FromUserId",
           "ToUserId",
           COUNT(*) AS "votes_from_to"
    FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
    WHERE "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
      AND "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY "FromUserId", "ToUserId"
)
SELECT *
FROM pair_cte
ORDER BY "votes_from_to" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Add the reverse direction to see “votes returned”.
WITH pair_cte AS (
    SELECT "FromUserId",
           "ToUserId",
           COUNT(*) AS "votes_from_to"
    FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
    WHERE "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
      AND "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY "FromUserId", "ToUserId"
)
SELECT a."FromUserId"       AS "giver",
       a."ToUserId"         AS "receiver",
       a."votes_from_to"    AS "votes_given",
       COALESCE(b."votes_from_to", 0) AS "votes_returned"
FROM pair_cte a
LEFT JOIN pair_cte b
       ON a."FromUserId" = b."ToUserId"
      AND a."ToUserId"   = b."FromUserId"
ORDER BY a."votes_given" DESC,
         "votes_returned" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Join with USERS table to attach usernames.
WITH pair_cte AS (
    SELECT "FromUserId",
           "ToUserId",
           COUNT(*) AS "votes_from_to"
    FROM "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."FORUMMESSAGEVOTES"
    WHERE "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
      AND "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY "FromUserId", "ToUserId"
),
paired AS (
    SELECT a."FromUserId"       AS "giver_id",
           a."ToUserId"         AS "rec_id",
           a."votes_from_to"    AS "votes_given",
           COALESCE(b."votes_from_to", 0) AS "votes_returned"
    FROM pair_cte a
    LEFT JOIN pair_cte b
           ON a."FromUserId" = b."ToUserId"
          AND a."ToUserId"   = b."FromUserId"
)
SELECT gu."UserName"  AS "giver_name",
       ru."UserName"  AS "receiver_name",
       p."votes_given",
       p."votes_returned"
FROM paired p
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."USERS" gu
  ON p."giver_id" = gu."Id"
JOIN "META_KAGGLE"."META_KAGGLE"."USERS" ru
  ON p."rec_id"   = ru."Id"
ORDER BY p."votes_given" DESC,
         p."votes_returned" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Restrict to pairs where at least one vote was reciprocated.
